# AAOS absorption boundary: preserve the archived donor bytes.
#
# The donor's own .gitattributes rules still win for the paths they name
# (including its three LF-normalized Markdown files, recorded in the manifest).
# This parent rule stops the host repository's core.autocrlf from rewriting
# donor files that have no explicit donor rule, so a Windows checkout keeps
# the same bytes that SOURCE-MANIFEST.json records.
** -text -eol -filter -diff -merge
